.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{Yea, so have I strived to preach the gospel, not where Christ was named, lest I should build upon another man's foundation:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textµBut as it is written,¦layout ‚¤textÙ-To whom he was not spoken of, they shall see:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ.And they that have not heard shall understand.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBFor which cause also I have been much hindered from coming to you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙiBut now having no more place in these parts, and having a great desire these many years to come unto you;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃwhensoever I take my journey into Spain, I will come to you: for I trust to see you in my journey, and to be brought on my way thitherward by you, if first I be somewhat filled with your company.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8But now I go unto Jerusalem to minister unto the saints.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{For it hath pleased them of Macedonia and Achaia to make a certain contribution for the poor saints which are at Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ»It hath pleased them verily; and their debtors they are. For if the Gentiles have been made partakers of their spiritual things, their duty is also to minister unto them in carnal things.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙhWhen therefore I have performed this, and have sealed to them this fruit, I will come by you into Spain.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnAnd I am sure that, when I come unto you, I shall come in the fulness of the blessing of the gospel of Christ.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book,§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNow I beseech you, brethren, for the Lord Jesus Christ's sake, and for the love of the Spirit, that ye strive together with me in your prayers to God for me;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙthat I may be delivered from them that do not believe in JudÃ¦a; and that my service which I have for Jerusalem may be accepted of the saints;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTthat I may come unto you with joy by the will of God, and may with you be refreshed.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book,§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse!¦verses‘„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ+Now the God of peace be with you all. Amen.¦layout ªlast_verse!